  "summary": "This experiment tested a unimodal RNA-only baseline (config_001) to compare against the multimodal config_016. Validation accuracy (48.5%) and F1 (46.4%) are lower than the multimodal baseline (52.7% accuracy, 51.0% F1), suggesting multimodal approaches may provide performance gains. However, the role of specific encoders, fusion strategies, and other configuration factors remains uncertain without further comparative analysis."
